tags: ergo-rest

A layer: the REST API of the Ergo reference node, over HTTP/1.1 with no TLS, on TCP. A
member of a proof-of-work network of Ergo gives it on one address.

The calls that a node uses are GET /info, GET /blocks/at/{height} and
GET /blocks/{id}/header. The answers are JSON, as the Ergo reference node gives them.
The port of the address selects the layer: nothing in TCP selects it.

A layer has no value.

=== formal
calls=GET /info, GET /blocks/at/{height}, GET /blocks/{id}/header
class=layer
name=ergo-rest
selected_by=the port of the address
spec=the REST API of the Ergo reference node (ergoplatform/ergo), HTTP/1.1, JSON, no TLS
transport=tcp
